```php
namespace App\Http\Middleware;

use Illuminate\Http\Request;

class AllowIP
{
    protected $allowedIPs = [
        '127.0.0.1', // localhost IP
        '192.168.1.1', // example network IP
    ];

    public function handle(Request $request, Closure $next)
    {
        $ip = $request->get('REMOTE_ADDR');

        if (!in_array($ip, $this->allowedIPs)) {
            throw new \Exception("IP address {$ip} is not allowed.");
        }

        return $next($request);
    }
}
```

In this middleware, we define an array of allowed IP addresses in the `$allowedIPs` property. The `handle` method retrieves the user's IP address from the request and checks if it exists in the `$allowedIPs` array. If the IP address is not allowed, we throw an exception to block the user.

